ket.AF_UNIX`. Once `mod.socket.AF_UNIX` is monkeypatched it compares against the patched value, not a host constant. Alternatively, explicitly assert `family == mod.socket.AF_UNIX` rather than dropping the family check.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py:48: `assert family == socket.AF_UNIX` reads the module attribute when the call happens, not a host value captured earlier","tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py:11 `import socket` and scripts/check_verify_host.py:20 `import socket` both point to the same sys.modules['socket'] object, so the setattr on mod.socket also patches the test's socket","scripts/check_verify_host.py:62,66: the probe calls `socket_factory(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)`, which reads the patched value"],"finding":"The plan says `_FakeSocket` needs to stop checking the family 'against the host constant'. That premise is false. `_FakeSocket.__init__` asserts `family == socket.AF_UNIX`, and since `mod.socket` is the same stdlib `socket` module the test imports, the planned `monkeypatch.setattr(mod.socket, \"AF_UNIX\", 1, raising=False)` also makes the test's `socket.AF_UNIX` equal 1. The probe passes `socket.AF_UNIX` (now 1), so the existing assertion would pass on Windows as it is. Removing it is unneeded and drops the only check that the probe really asks for an AF_UNIX socket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f937c8639285d643f","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — '_FakeSocket stops asserting the family value against the host constant' (tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py:47-48)","norm_id":"n7349f75029e5ecdf","priority":0.55,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["After the change, a regression where the probe passes AF_INET (or some other family) to the factory would no longer be caught by the fake-socket tests on any platform."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Remove the clause '_FakeSocket stops asserting the family value against the host constant' from Approach. If you want it to be explicit, change the assertion to `assert family == mod.socket.AF_UNIX`. That still holds after the setattr and keeps the check that the probe asks for an AF_UNIX socket.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Keep `_FakeSocket`'s family check and point it at the probe module's patched attribute (`assert family == mod.socket.AF_UNIX`) instead of removing it. It is read at call time, so it holds on Windows once the test sets AF_UNIX.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"and `_FakeSocket` stops asserting the family value against the host constant.\"","tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py:11 `import socket` and :48 `assert family == socket.AF_UNIX`. The attribute is looked up when the fake is called, not at import time.","scripts/check_verify_host.py:20 `import socket` and :62/:66 `socket_factory(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)`. This is the same stdlib module object the test patches."],"finding":"The plan has `_FakeSocket` stop asserting the family 'against the host constant', but that assertion doesn't depend on the host. Line 48, `assert family == socket.AF_UNIX`, looks up `socket.AF_UNIX` when the fake is constructed. The test's `socket` is the same module object as `mod.socket`, so once `monkeypatch.setattr(mod.socket, \"AF_UNIX\", 1, raising=False)` runs, the lookup returns the patched 1 and the assertion passes on Windows unchanged. Deleting it means the tests no longer check that the probe opens an AF_UNIX socket, and that check costs nothing to keep.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1e6f78305c9d1af7","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — first bullet ('`_FakeSocket` stops asserting the family value against the host constant'); tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py:47-48","norm_id":"n4ebd24aa334d2768","priority":0.55,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit makes the probe open a socket with the wrong family, for example AF_INET. Without the assertion, the fake-socket tests still pass on every platform.","On Windows, after the plan's setattr, the existing assertion already passes (1 == 1), so removing it fixes nothing."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the Approach, replace '`_FakeSocket` stops asserting the family value against the host constant' with '`_FakeSocket` keeps its family check, written as `assert family == mod.socket.AF_UNIX`, which reads the value the test patched'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Keep a family check in `_FakeSocket` that asserts the requested family equals the value the test installed (e.g. `mod.socket.AF_UNIX` read at call time, or a distinct sentinel), instead of dropping the check entirely.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"`_FakeSocket` stops asserting the family value against the host constant\"","Taxonomy item 4 (fixture invalidity): without this assertion, the fixture no longer exercises the claim that the probe uses an AF_UNIX socket."],"finding":"The approach says `_FakeSocket` stops asserting the family value against the host constant, but replaces that check with nothing. After the change, neither fake-socket test verifies that the probe opens its socket with AF_UNIX, so a regression to the wrong family would still pass. The family assertion can be kept portably: compare it to the value the test itself installs, which is `mod.socket.AF_UNIX` after the monkeypatch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff822cf80b3600c91","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — first bullet (_FakeSocket family assertion)","norm_id":"n13fdd6574460dba2","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The probe is later changed to call `socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, ...)` or to omit the family. The fake accepts it, and both tests stay green on every platform."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In each fake-socket test, set a sentinel with `monkeypatch.setattr(mod.socket, \"AF_UNIX\", sentinel, raising=False)` and pass it to `_FakeSocket`, or have `_FakeSocket.__init__` assert `family == mod.socket.AF_UNIX`, read when the fake is constructed. This holds on every host, because the attribute is always the test-installed value.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Keep _FakeSocket's family check, comparing against the patched `mod.socket.AF_UNIX` read at call time rather than a host constant, so the tests still prove the probe requests AF_UNIX on every platform.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'_FakeSocket stops asserting the family value against the host constant'","'monkeypatch.setattr(mod.socket, \"AF_UNIX\", 1, raising=False)'","Goal stated as 'Make the 3 tests set the platform condition they test instead of inheriting it from the host', which is a portability fix, not a reduction in what the tests check."],"finding":"The plan removes _FakeSocket's address-family assertion instead of retargeting it. The tests then no longer verify that unix_socket_probe opens an AF_UNIX socket, which weakens the very behavior they exist to check. Because the AF_UNIX patch is applied to `mod.socket`, the same module object the fake sees, a family check read at call time against `mod.socket.AF_UNIX` (the patched sentinel 1) would pass on every platform.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5caaa3e0847ea17b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — '_FakeSocket stops asserting the family value against the host constant'","norm_id":"n8b5137efc3830b7f","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future regression makes unix_socket_probe create the socket with the wrong family (e.g. AF_INET). The fake-socket tests still pass on macOS, Linux and Windows because nothing checks the family anymore."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In _FakeSocket.__init__, replace the host-constant comparison with `assert family == mod.socket.AF_UNIX` evaluated at construction time. Alternatively, record `family` and assert in each test that it equals the sentinel value set via monkeypatch (1).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the evidence for the no-skip criterion: run `pytest tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py -rs` on macOS, and record the module's skipped count (0) from the Windows sweep job log alongside the run id.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"macOS: the module passes.\"","\"Windows: ... shows the 3 tests passing, recorded here\"","No step names a check that reports skipped tests (e.g. pytest `-rs` summary or a skip count)."],"finding":"The acceptance criterion 'No test in the module is skipped on any platform' has no proving command or named evidence. The Testing section only says 'the module passes' on macOS and that 'the 3 tests passing' in the Windows run will be recorded. Neither shows a skip count of zero, and pytest reports skipped tests as non-failing, so a run can be green with skips.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f447a6399047d6bc8","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'No test in the module is skipped on any platform'; Testing section","norm_id":"naa898b3d7b01b374","priority":0.165,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Someone later adds a `skipif(sys.platform == 'win32')` to make a test green. The recorded Windows run still shows 'passed' for the module, and this criterion is never actually checked."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Testing: on macOS, run `pytest tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py -rs -v` and confirm the summary line has no 'skipped'. For Windows, record the dispatched run/job id and quote the 3 test ids as PASSED, plus 0 skips for the module (e.g. via `-rs` output or a `grep -c SKIPPED` over the module's lines in the job log).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Dispatch by file